    {
      "id": "51174",
      "entry": {
        "title": "CFA2438-R-s03-Q9",
        "feedback": {
          "correct": "",
          "neutral": "<p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">C is correct.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">Using the information provided, the periodic <em>PMT</em> is equal to</p>\n<div id=\"CFA2438-R-s03-E___27\" style=\"margin-left: 1.618em; overflow-x: auto; padding: 10px 0;\"><math><semantics> <mrow> <mstyle><mfrac> <mrow> <mo>(</mo> <mi>M</mi> <mi>R</mi> <mi>R</mi> <mo>+</mo> <mi>Q</mi> <mi>M</mi> <mo>)</mo> <mo>×</mo> <mi>F</mi> <mi>V</mi> </mrow> <mi>m</mi> </mfrac></mstyle> <mo>=</mo> <mstyle><mfrac> <mrow> <mo>(</mo> <mo>−</mo> <mn>0.055</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>0.016</mn> <mo>)</mo> <mo>×</mo> <mn>100</mn> </mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mfrac></mstyle> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0.2625.</mn> </mrow> </semantics></math></div>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">Using the RATE function in Microsoft Excel, Google Sheets, or a financial calculator and using <em>PV</em> = –101.20, <em>FV</em> = 100, <em>PMT</em> =0.275, and <em>N</em> = 8, we solve for the discount rate per period of 0.11175%. The discount margin can then be estimated by solving for <em>DM</em>:</p>\n<div id=\"CFA2438-R-s03-E___28\" style=\"margin-left: 1.618em; overflow-x: auto; padding: 10px 0;\"><math><semantics> <mrow> <mi>r</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mstyle><mfrac> <mrow> <mi>M</mi> <mi>R</mi> <mi>R</mi> <mo>+</mo> <mi>D</mi> <mi>M</mi> </mrow> <mi>m</mi> </mfrac></mstyle> <mo>.</mo> </mrow> </semantics></math></div>\n<div id=\"CFA2438-R-s03-E___29\" style=\"margin-left: 1.618em; overflow-x: auto; padding: 10px 0;\"><math><semantics> <mrow> <mn>0.0011175</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mstyle><mfrac> <mrow> <mo>−</mo> <mn>0.0055</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mi>D</mi> <mi>M</mi> </mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mfrac></mstyle> <mo>.</mo> </mrow> </semantics></math></div>\n<div id=\"CFA2438-R-s03-E___30\" style=\"margin-left: 1.618em; overflow-x: auto; padding: 10px 0;\"><math><semantics> <mrow> <mi>D</mi> <mi>M</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0.9970%.</mn> </mrow> </semantics></math></div>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">The estimated discount margin is 99.7 bps.</p>",
          "incorrect": ""
        },
        "itemBody": "<p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">A two-year floating-rate note issued by a French corporation pays the three-month MRR of –0.55% plus 160 bps. The floater is priced at 101.20 per 100 of par value. Assuming the 30/360 day-count convention and 90 days per period and a flat yield curve, the discount margin for the floater is closest to:</p>",
