      "id": "51176",
      "entry": {
        "body": "<p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">A fixed-income portfolio manager is looking to value a one-year US dollar–denominated floating-rate note that has quarterly payments based on 90-day MRR plus 80 bps. Assume the following information:</p><ul id=\"CFA2438-R-s03-L3\" style=\"list-style-type: none; margin-bottom: 15px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n               <li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 10px; position: relative;\">\n                  <p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">90-Day MRR: 2.5%</p>\n               </li>\n               <li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 10px; position: relative;\">\n                  <p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">Quoted Margin: 80 bps</p>\n               </li>\n               <li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 10px; position: relative;\">\n                  <p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">Discount Margin: 100 bps</p>\n               </li>\n               <li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 10px; position: relative;\">\n                  <p style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\">Face Value: USD100</p>\n               </li>\n            </ul>",
