    {
      "id": "53814",
      "entry": {
        "title": "ITEM_20170607058",
        "feedback": {},
        "itemBody": "<p>DMT Corp. issued a five-year floating-rate note (FRN) that pays a quarterly coupon of three-month market reference rate (MRR) plus 125 bps. The FRN is priced at 96 per 100 of par value. Assuming a 30/360-day count convention, evenly spaced periods, and constant three-month market reference rate (MRR) of 5%, the discount margin for the FRN is <i>closest</i> to:</p>",
        "properties": {
          "shuffleRules": {
            "choices": {
              "toLock": [],
              "shuffled": false
            }
          },
          "varyPointsByAnswer": false
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "f5a48852-a73a-40f1-80ce-93c24b8319dc"
        },
        "answerFeedback": {
          "122e777b-2929-48c3-a725-9dd4b1929f87": "<p>Incorrect because it uses the quarterly discount rate 1.8025% as the solution, i.e., 180 bps.</p>",
          "587dcc93-7e1d-4539-89cb-3c52464efd58": "<p>Incorrect because it uses the price discount of 100% – 96% = 4%, i.e., 400 bps.</p>",
          "f5a48852-a73a-40f1-80ce-93c24b8319dc": "<p><strong>Correct</strong> because the interest payment each period per 100 of par value is</p>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 1.618em;\"><math style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><semantics> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mtext>Index</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>×</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow> <mi>m</mi> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mn>0.05</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.0125</mn></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>×</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo><mn>1.5625</mn></mrow></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Where index is the market reference rate</p>\n<p>The discount margin can be estimated by solving for <em>DM</em> in the equation</p>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 1.618em;\"><math style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><semantics> <mrow> <mn>96</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1.5625</mn></mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mn>0.05</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>+</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1.5625</mn></mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mn>0.05</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>+</mo><mo>⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1.5625</mn></mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mn>0.05</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> <mrow> <mn>20</mn></mrow> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The solution for the discount rate, <em>r</em> = (0.05 + <em>DM</em>)/4 is 1.8025%. Therefore, <em>DM</em> = 2.21% or 221 bps.</p>"
        },
