        "answerFeedback": {
          "76eca831-04d3-42ec-a52e-11f5755bda48": "<p>Incorrect. To calculate the bond equivalent yield: <em>FV</em> = 100, Days = 90, Year = 360, <em>DR</em> = 0.0578.</p><p style=\"margin-left:1.618em\"><em>PV</em> = 100 × [1 – (90/360) × 0.0578] = 98.555</p><p style=\"margin-left:1.618em\"><em>AOR</em> = (365/90) × [(100 – 98.555)/98.555] = 5.946%</p>",
          "8d109f2b-4482-4962-ba45-681b8409b57c": "<p>Incorrect. To calculate the bond equivalent yield: <em>FV</em> = 100, Days = 90, Year = 365, <em>DR</em> = 0.058.</p><p style=\"margin-left:1.618em\"><em>PV</em> = 100 × [1 – (90/365) × 0.058] = 98.570</p><p style=\"margin-left:1.618em\"><em>AOR</em> = (365/90) × [(100 – 98.570)/98.5705] = 5.883%</p>",
          "9418cfd4-ed40-46a2-ac2b-a8d4f6eb1470": "<p><strong>Correct.</strong> Instrument C provides a bond equivalent yield of 5.96%, compared with 5.946% for Instrument A and 5.883% for Instrument B.</p>"
        },
